{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":30000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"da40bcff021941cbb9b708beec3d372c047383960abfa4f3bf429a598183415a","packTokens":6551,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":1,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":706,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"intent","tokens":330,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":428,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"assumptions","tokens":98,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"cb","tokens":1972,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"request","tokens":2915,"trimmed":false,"trust":"untrusted"},{"id":"task","tokens":11,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"specify"},"pointers":[],"system":"Senior engineer writing a behaviour spec a test author can turn into black-box tests.\nFormat rules (checked by code):\n- Each requirement is one EARS sentence with exactly one \"shall\": \"The <system> shall ...\", \"When <trigger>, the <system> shall ...\", \"While <state>, the <system> shall ...\", \"Where <feature>, the <system> shall ...\", \"If <condition>, then the <system> shall ...\". IDs REQ-1, REQ-2...\n- op = ADDED | MODIFIED | REMOVED, the change to the existing code, not to this spec. MODIFIED and REMOVED copy their anchors exactly from the current-behaviour claims.\n- Each requirement has ≥1 acceptance criterion AC-<req>.<n> in Given/When/Then, observable at a public surface: a public class method called directly, an HTTP call, a job run, an outbound call to a named system, a DB row, or a screen. level: unit | api | job | ui | manual.\n- Each Then names what a test reads, using at least one of these words: response, status, returned, row, record, call, request, sent, email, message, error, event, field, value, count, list, file, screen, page, shown, displayed. \"Sign-in succeeds\" fails; \"The response status is 200\" passes. (manual criteria are exempt.)\n- Pick the LOWEST level that proves the behaviour: unit when the logic lives in one class (cal